de in the answer can be inferred from the con- text. To estimate faithfulness, we first use an LLM to extract a set of statements, S(as(q))."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_2e7f7273fa816f48","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":14,"quote":"Conversely, the expansion of context provides new opportunities for the development of RAG, enabling it to address more complex problems and integrative or summary questions that require reading a large amount of material to answer [49]."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_d50bb188f7f3bf9f","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":12,"quote":"Longrope: Extending llm context window beyond 2 million tokens."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_d125f8e7fcbac0e3","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"Finally, we demonstrate that the non-parametric memory can be replaced to update the models’ knowledge as the world changes.1 2 Methods We explore RAG models, which use the input sequence x to retrieve text documents z and use them as"},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_6c09d8a99edf7cbd","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":12,"quote":"Answer Faithfulness ensures that the generated answers remain true to the retrieved context, maintaining consistency and avoiding contradictions."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_8240c2e11040036d","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":26,"quote":"Since the only concept tagged by HippoRAG is “protons”, it extracts passages related to “Uranium” and “nuclear weapons” while ColBERTv2 uses the context to extract more relevant passages associated with the discovery of atomic numbers."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_3e66e086bac3b1f0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":25,"quote":"This occurs when multiple passages exist in the corpus that discuss very similar topics since the PPR algorithm is not able to leverage query context directly."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_2a755a4c670482cd","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":12,"quote":"Data engineering for scaling language models to 128k context, 2024."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_18d51945e91f5002","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"Facing complex issues, a single retrieval based on the original query may not suffice to acquire adequate context information."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_565b7707a80ea104","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"Complex datasets (e.g., Wikipedia) typically require large schemas that exceed the context window length or can be ig- nored by the LLMs (Wadhwa et al., 2023)."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f2896d5f55e04d17","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":4,"quote":"The Predict module aims to reduce redundancy and noise by generating context directly through the LLM, ensuring relevance and accuracy [13]."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_5a8ae7af32a9d1fc","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"In generating responses, the model may face the issue of hallucination, where it produces con- tent not supported by the retrieved context."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_3208ec013026edaf","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":10,"quote":"Context Curation Redundant information can interfere with the final gener- ation of LLM, and overly long contexts can also lead LLM to the “Lost in the middle” problem [98]."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_55fd9d2fefae9c4f","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":17,"quote":"When tested on Wiki-NRE, which has a moderately-sized schema, EDC already signifi- cantly outperforms the baseline methods, poten- tially due to the confusion of the LLMs when deal- ing with long context (Liu et al., 2024)."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_05a521270f216026","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"To accommodate the context limitations of language models, text is segmented into smaller, digestible chunks."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_3fa0659d7f419fcb","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":3,"quote":"These chunks are subsequently used as the expanded context in prompt."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_6c09d8a99edf7cbd","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":12,"quote":"Context Relevance evaluates the precision and specificity of the retrieved context, ensuring relevance and minimizing processing costs associated with extraneous content."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_edf44178ff442ebf","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":1,"quote":"This early stage was characterized by foundational work aimed at refining pre-training techniques [3]–[5].The subsequent arrival of ChatGPT [6] marked a pivotal moment, with LLM demonstrating powerful in context learning (ICL) capabilities."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_63b70d30e6c602f7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"The quality of index construction determines whether the correct context can be obtained in the retrieval phase."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_9b547c3112507803","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":1,"quote":"VectorRAG excels in situations where context from related textual documents is crucial for generating meaningful and coherent responses [9–11]."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"6c24762a3f277fd1_c_b111edc0d96e0395","docId":"6c24762a3f277fd1","docTitle":"2309.15217_Ragas_Automated_Evaluation_of_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":3,"quote":"Faithfulness We say that the answer as(q) is faithful to the context c(q) if the claims that are made in the answer can be inferred from the con- text."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_3025ebdcb9ebb485","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":19,"quote":"Given such, we expect that triples that contain any of these entities or are nearby in the graph should provide helpful context."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_3e66e086bac3b1f0","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":25,"quote":"Context Tradeoff Given our method’s entity-centric nature in extraction and indexing, it has a strong bias towards concepts that leaves many contextual signals unused."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_8f3a31bea776841b","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":8,"quote":"Retrieval datasets: Apart from the context of RAG, several benchmarking datasets exist for in- formation retrieval evaluation."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_dde6285270dd3d03","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":17,"quote":"Generate rather than retrieve: Large language models are strong context generators."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_4805baae415f96b7","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":5,"quote":"MS-MARCO SotA is [4], FEVER-3 is [68] and FEVER-2 is [57] *Uses gold context/evidence."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_7f152473f08f904b","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":5,"quote":"Datasets like FinanceBench5 provides question-context-answer triplets but they are not useful as here we are comparing VectorRAG, GraphRAG and HybridRAG and they do not provide the context generated from a KG."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_a4ae74d37afdb029","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":74,"quote":"Large language models can be easily distracted by irrelevant context."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"6c24762a3f277fd1_c_b3d41f0162312809","docId":"6c24762a3f277fd1","docTitle":"2309.15217_Ragas_Automated_Evaluation_of_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":5,"quote":"To put the results in context, we compare our proposed metrics (shown as Ragas in Table 1) with two baseline methods."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_abde3fe7a5bc7ca6","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":83,"quote":"Making retrieval-augmented language models robust to irrelevant context."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_7344ee79eac80571","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"Never- theless, these approaches still cannot strike a balance between semantic completeness and context length."},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_2a290f0c5ab18fd1","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":4,"quote":"2.4.3 Context Precision."},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_74ae59804122cb69","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":11,"quote":"SearchQA: A New Q&A Dataset Augmented with Context from a Search Engine."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_2e7f7273fa816f48","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":14,"quote":"G is still necessary when LLMs 8https://www.trulens.org/trulens eval/core concepts rag triad/ 9https://kimi.moonshot.cn are not constrained by context."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_2e7f7273fa816f48","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":14,"quote":"On one hand, providing LLMs with a large amount of context at once will significantly impact its inference speed, while chunked retrieval and on-demand input can significantly improve operational efficiency."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_2e7f7273fa816f48","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":14,"quote":"The entire retrieval and reasoning process is observable, while generation solely rely